The viable route is Track B, not Track A. I’m using the paper’s polynomial nonnegative rank-one regime honestly: instances are integer matrices \(M=uv^\top+E\) with a composed zero-marginal perturbation \(E\). A general solver can use the paper’s linear-feasibility method; the compact route is the hidden row/column-total invariant, and verification remains exact rational arithmetic. I’m now stress-testing whether the paper’s own alternating minimax heuristic makes this distribution too easy before committing it to the module.
