The existing draft has a real G8 defect: every seed uses the same cyclic support system, and independent Boolean-variable complementation carries any planted right-hand side to any other. So the claimed 20-way diversity is presentation-only. I’m fixing that by adding seed-dependent, same-format parity supports while retaining a recoverable cyclic backbone; the canonical key will ignore RHS values, include the support hypergraph, and explicitly test signed-variable relabellings. I’ll also replace the estimated compact cost with an executable recurrence solver and measured XOR count.
