+def _make_xor_rows(base_values, rng, decoys):
+    """Make a full-rank cyclic backbone plus seed-dependent parity supports.
+
+    Every added support has three previously unused variable pairs.  Thus the
+    pairs occurring twice are exactly the adjacent pairs of the cyclic
+    backbone.  Added rows are constraints, not fake clauses: their right-hand
+    sides are evaluated on the already sampled witness.  The backbone alone is
+    nonsingular because its length is not divisible by three.
