codex
A mandatory standard attack just killed the draft: native NAE unit-propagation DPLL solves all eight shipping instances in only 5–30 search nodes. That makes the Gaussian-versus-recurrence story false—the mechanical route is actually shorter than the claimed compact one. I’m checking whether this is caused by the redundant supports or is intrinsic to the cyclic encoding; if intrinsic, this family must be rejected rather than cosmetically hardened.
exec
/bin/bash -lc "python3 - <<'PY'
import gen_1706_00078 as g,time
for n in (23,35,47,59,71,83,95):
 if n%3==0: continue
 for d in (0, min(n//2, 24), 2*n):
  nodes=[]; solved=0
  for s in range(8):
   i=g.make_instance(n=n,decoys=d,seed=100+s)
