The bare loop finished with `budget_bound`: every level through 26 bits and 52 extra equations was solved, so this is not shippable at the current ladder, but the script explicitly says not to reject because the next cap-compliant size still exists. The fixed-length decoy axis was empirically counterproductive, so I’m testing the allowed next axis—56 base bits, still only 278 XORs and 56 output bits—in an isolated script-owned trial before deciding whether the paper can be hardened or must remain parked.
