The 58-bit call could not run because the shared key hit its total quota, but the 56-bit near-cap instance had already been solved, and the full bare transcript solved every tested level. This family therefore fails H on Track B even though G and V pass. I’m preserving the built module as a rejected prototype, recording both the 8,123-operation mechanical route and 128/278-operation compact routes, and keeping the script-owned evidence rather than claiming a hardened generator.
