741:We observed in practice that, in this case, Algorithm~\ref{altopt} is always able to converge to an optimal solution. Optimality can be verified by checking that the answer to D-$\ell_\infty$-R1A($M_q$,$f^*-\epsilon$) is NO, where $f^*$ is the objective function value of Algorithm~\ref{altopt} at convergence and $\epsilon$ is a small positive constant. (We have included this function in the code available online.) 
