X = 0$.\n\nSubstituting $X = 0$ back into our expressions yields the exact bit for each variable:\n- Variables equal to 0: $y_1, y_2, y_6, y_7, y_8, y_9, y_{12}, y_{14}, y_{15}, y_{21}$\n- Variables equal to 1: $y_0, y_3, y_4, y_5, y_{10}, y_{11}, y_{13}, y_{16}, y_{17}, y_{18}, y_{19}, y_{20}, y_{22}, y_{23}, y_{24}, y_{25}$\n\nWriting these 26 values in order from $y_0$ to $y_{25}$:\n\n<answer>10011100001101001111101111</answer>", "error": null, "elapsed_sec": 78.69, "http_status": 200, "finish_reason": "stop", "preset": "escalated", "escalation_round": 5}
